Well, I should have ascended in the meantime :-).  I first tried a few 
undead slayers, but did not get far with them.  They are pretty weak in 
the beginning, and I seem to have lost lots of my good instincts since 
the time I played more regularly.  Then I decided to do something easy, 
a barbarian.  He descended and got powerful very fast and picked up a 
cockatrice in Sokaban not wearing gloves...  Normally, when I am that 
powerful, I have already read a scroll of enchant armor, that is I have 
stripped at least once, and then I always test whether I have my gloves 
on, before picking up a 'trice.  This time, I had an AC of about -10 but 
  not having stripped before, I somehow assumed implicitly I was wearing 
gloves... (See what I mean about instincts?)

My next barbarian would have made it; I am convinced of this, because he 
had already done Demogorgon.  But when he switched levels, the game 
crashed.  He survived, according to the DYWYPI-screens, but is still 
listed as having died by a trickery in the game record.  This was 
version 007E6F2, so I decided downloading 007E6F3, the latest version, 
hoping it would be more stable.  Started a monk that seemed even easier 
than the barbarian and who died from a trickery, when he started looking 
good, but still well inside the dungeon.

Finally, I realized that on my home computer, I would have to make a 
backup file after each change to a new level, if I ever wanted to 
ascend, to use it in guise of a recover program.  This is tedious, but 
it was necessary.  I have another monk who has finished the castle.  I 
had to revive him seven times after trickeries so far.  Of course, I hit 
"q" every time the game asks me "DYWYPI?" after a trickery.

In order to see whether the same problem is present on linux machines, I 
downloaded and compiled the game on one.  There I have an ascendable 
valkyrie running and the game so far has not crashed on me (of course, I 
do backups here, too, just to make sure; I don't want to lose hours of 
gameplay again to a bug).  However, my history with valks in slashem 
makes me blush.  In nethack, I think I could ascend one out of two 
valks.  In slashem, it is only the seventh that is still alive.  The 
sixth was doing pretty well but died a stupid death by falling into lava 
in Sokoban (at an AC of -15, which in nethack is almost a guaranteed 
ascension).  I had taken the lava pool for a fountain... (no colors, 
unfortunately, in that tty version).  Nevertheless, the fact that both 
the sixth and seventh became strong, seems to show that my instincts are 
coming back...  Still, valkyries are more difficult in slashem than in 
nethack, since they only get a +1 spear instead of a long sword 
initially.  This is only one damage point difference on average, but 
together with the fact that tougher monsters can appear earlier in 
slashem, it seems to matter a lot.  In any case, in slashem, barbarians 
seem to be way easier to me than valks, but the easiest class is the 
monk (at least in the main dungeon).

