genocided arch lichs already or I did not approach the statue of an arch 
  lich on an island there.  If arch-lichs are not extinct, that statue 
comes alive!  (Maybe only with a certain probability.)  It almost killed 
my valkyrie number seven, mostly due to the fact that you cannot hit it 
with unenchanted weapons.  But +1 is sufficient on an artifact weapon. 
My Mjollnir was at +1...  Still, it did not do any lightning damage and 
without the wand of death to get rid of the summoned green dragon 
(dragons are - appropriately - much more dangerous than in nethack) and 
a potion of full healing, the arch lich would have been the demise of 
poor Gwen.

I also have visited Frankenstein's lab in hell twice, once in an explore 
mode game and once in the game of the barbarian who was tricked 
afterwards.  And of course, I have done the whole game in explore mode, 
so I know more or less what to expect in the demon's lairs.  One danger, 
to which I have no good answer with a monk yet is the spell that creates 
a pool.  In a demon's lair without the possibility to teleport that will 
be an instakill, if you are already surrounded by monsters which is 
pretty likely due to preceding spells.  So you should either levitate 
all the time, which greatly reduces the efficiency of your best weapon, 
an assault rifle shooting normally five bullets at a time (each doing 
d30 + enchantment damage; for demon lords, they should be enchanted to 
+4), or fly, which means to polymorph into an unfavourable form 
(vampire) or wear an amulet of flying which is not good, if you need the 
amulet of reflection, or you have to wear water walking boots, which 
deprives you of speed, unless you keep casting haste self or quaffing 
potions of speed.  Gauntlets of swimming take away the huge boost in AC 
offered by gauntlets of dexterity; also I am not sure whether you will 
not still soak your bag of holding when falling into a pool with 
gauntlets of swimming.  Moreover, in Gehennom pools might (I don't know 
that really) be filled with water from Lethe (the castle moat is), which 
has a more desastrous effect on your potions and scrolls and has a 
mind-flayer-like effect on yourself...  I guess, if I can't find a 
shield of reflection (which may not be useful for my monk anyway), I 
will chose the water walking boots...

