> There seem to be some balance issues with Slash'em, I suppose?

Yes.  It is more difficult in the beginning and, possibly, easier in the 
end, because you have so many opportunities to get powerful equipment 
that you depend much less on the RNG.  For a lawful, the end game is 
easy, as he can get extremely powerful pets by sacrificing - the 
aforementioned Planetars.  I don't know whether neutrals or chaotics 
have similar advantages.  My neutrals got elementals only, so far.  Air 
elementals are the worst, they attack everything and therefore die 
easily.  Moreover, elementals are not visible by telepathy, so you don't 
know where your pets are.  Chaotics initially get shadow wolves and the 
like, later demons.  Maybe if they can get to balrogs, they will also 
have powerful pets, but still a far way from Planetars.

Still I think the balance issue is not a major one.  Slashem is less 
balanced than nethack, but a good player will not ascend *significantly* 
less frequently.  It is mostly a question of knowing how to deal with 
different kinds of difficulties.  An exception are some of the new 
classes such as lycanthropes.  I tried one in explore mode and gave up 
on it.  I guess, I would need about thirty games to ascend my first 
lycanthrope.  And it would be a matter of luck to a large extent, 
because you just need a ring of polymorph control to play that class 
decently.  Therefore, I am somewhat discouraged playing one of them, not 
wanting to depend on luck too much...

